      "message": "\"See if the test runs on the dev board (bloonchipper/dartmonkey would be good to test with since we know those boards are in good working condition.)\"\nThe test doesn\u0027t compile on bloonchipper/dartmonkey in its current form. Adding code changes to work around errors exposed other problems (so far).\n\n\"The fpsensor_auth_crypto_stateful test is a different test than what I was referring to. It sounds like that one was broken too and is exercising some of the new code indirectly. \"\nThis unit test call the get_ikm function, where the bulk of the changes were made, directly. So, not sure what you mean by indirectly? If we need additional test coverage in a unit test, wouldn\u0027t it be simpler to modify the test that is already running on hardware and working rather than trying to refresh a test (fpsensor_crypto) which hasn\u0027t been running on fingerprint hardware for some time?",
